/ActualText (OVER THE SHOULDER WIDE\r\n\rWider environmental fashion portrait of the same woman seated inside a recessed white architectural lounge surrounded by the swimming pool. The camera is positioned behind and slightly above her.\r Her wet back faces the camera while she turns her head over one shoulder and makes quiet eye contact with the lens.\r One knee is raised toward her body while one arm rests loosely across it.\r Minimal taupe swimwear is visible naturally from the back.\r Wet hair falls in separated strands down the center of her back.\r One sculptural gold flower earring remains clearly visible against her jawline.\r Large white angular pool walls create strong diagonal lines throughout the frame.\r Turquoise water forms the background while blurred Mediterranean vegetation and pale blue sky appear softly in the distance.\r Bright sunlight falls across her shoulders and upper back, revealing realistic water droplets, freckles and natural skin variations.\r\nCamera: 50mm lens, f/2.5.  \r\nEnvironmental fashion portrait with moderately shallow depth of field and subtle film grain.\r\n\r\n\nDIRECT GAZE\r\n\rFront-facing poolside portrait of the same model.\r She remains low inside the pool and leans both forearms horizontally across a thick white stone pool ledge.\r Her hands overlap naturally in front of her while her chin rests just above them.\r She looks directly into the camera with a relaxed, almost expressionless editorial gaze.\r Her shoulders and arms are wet and covered with small irregular water droplets.\r Both gold flower earrings appear on either side of her face, partially emerging from the wet hair.\r Her face sits near the center of the composition.\r Her forearms create a strong horizontal foreground line while the white architectural ledge fills the lower portion of the image.\r Turquoise swimming pool water and white architectural elements recede softly into the background.\r Direct summer sunlight produces realistic highlights across her forehead and cheeks while one side of the face falls into a subtle natural shadow.\r\nCamera: 85mm lens, f/2.  \r\nFocus precisely on the eyes with realistic background separation and analogue texture.\r\n\r\n\nREALISM LOCK\r\n\rAdd this section to the end of every prompt.\r The final image must look physically photographed rather than AI generated.\r Preserve small photographic inconsistencies: uneven water droplets, imperfect wet hair strands, subtle facial asymmetry, visible pores, peach fuzz, slight redness, freckles, natural skin translucency and minor texture variations.\r Include slight lens softness, organic shadow falloff, optical highlight blooming, occasional clipped highlights, restrained contrast and fine photographic grain.\r Avoid waxy skin, excessive sharpness, HDR, perfect symmetry, fake bokeh, synthetic-looking water, perfectly smooth architecture, beauty retouching, CGI jewelry and overly polished commercial rendering.\r The image should feel like a real editorial photograph captured on location.\r\n\r\n\nPRODUCT PRESERVATION\r\n\rWhen using a real jewelry product as a reference image, add:\r\n\rUse the uploaded jewelry image as the exact product reference. Preserve its original silhouette, proportions, petal count, surface texture, material, color and construction. Do not redesign, simplify, enlarge, shrink or reinterpret the jewelry. Maintain the same product identity across every image in the campaign.**\r\n\r\n\nCONSISTENCY TIP\r\n\rFor a complete campaign, generate the strongest hero image first.\r Use that image as a visual reference for the remaining scenes whenever the model allows reference-image conditioning.\r\n\r\nModel identity \267 Jewelry \267 Hair \267 Makeup \267 Skin tone \267 Location \267 Swimwear \267 Lighting direction \267 Color palette\n\r\nChange only the pose, framing and camera perspective from image to image.\r\n\r\n9 prompts. One visual world.\(\nBuilt for campaigns that never needed a photoshoot. &\r\n\r\n)
